LOCATED FIX SITE(S) — traced in this repository before you were asked. Anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces:
- src/services/contentstack.ts :: options — Central Contentstack Stack initialization. The `options` object passed to `contentstack.Stack(options)` is where `live_preview` config (preview_token, host) must be added. Currently has no live_preview config at all — this is the primary attachment point for enabling Live Preview SDK support.
- src/services/pageService.ts :: getPageContent — The main page-level data fetcher that calls getEntry/getSingletonEntry/findSingletonEntry for all page content types. Preview mode must be detected at the page level and threaded through these calls so draft entries are returned during Live Preview sessions.
- src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx — The catch-all Pages Router page that renders all Contentstack-driven pages. This is where preview-mode detection must occur (checking for Contentstack live-preview query parameters like live_preview and content_type_uid) and where the preview context gets passed into the data-fetching layer.
- src/services/partnersPromotionsService.ts — Bypasses the centralized ContentstackFactory by calling `Stack.ContentType(type)` directly. These direct Stack calls also need `.includeDraft()` in preview mode. Same pattern applies to stationService.ts, blogService.ts, and userAccountService.ts which also call Stack.ContentType directly.
- src/interface/contentstack.ts :: ICreateQueryConfig — The TypeScript interfaces that define the shape of query configurations. `ICreateQueryConfig`, `ICreateEntryConfig`, `IContentstackGetEntry`, `IContentstackGetSingleEntry`, `IContentstackGetSingletonEntry` must all be extended with an optional `includeDraft` boolean so the draft flag can flow through the type system from page detection to Stack query.


